Good morning. Yumeiro Pâtissière is brought to you by Konami and these other sponsors.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:57.920
Green Cape
Nikoniko Farm

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:03.330
There sure are quite a few people here.

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:06.980
This is a farm that is orientated towards visitors.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.470
Huh? What's wrong, Amano?

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:10.930
Wow!!!

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:16.440
Special Milk

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:16.440
Nikoniko

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:16.440
Farm

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:16.440
Gelato

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:16.440
Soft Serve Ice Cream

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:14.190
Soft serve ice cream! Packaged gelato! All fresh!

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:16.440
Hey, Amano! We didn't come here to <i>eat</i> the food!

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:18.060
Oh man, which one should I eat?? Let's hurry inside!

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:19.650
It's just like Amano-san.

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:35.120
Though I'm well-matched with roses, steeds also suit me quite well.

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:40.210
So cool!

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:41.880
My knight in shining armour!

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:45.550
Thank you.

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:47.860
Here, these are the meals for the sheep.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:49.600
Please give these to the sheep.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:52.980
Both of them have really forgotten about what we've come here for.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:56.020
Here! Some for you too.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:05:01.270
Note: <i>boku</i> is a "you" that is used to address young boys, which makes Kashino upset.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:56.760
Huh?

00:04:58.090 --> 00:05:01.270
Who are you calling "you"!? I'm already twelve!

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:02.840
Oh my, I'm sorry.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:04.130
Because I look short, huh?

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:06.130
Whoa! What are you doing-

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:07.740
...a sheep?

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:10.930
You want it?

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:12.020
Here.

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:15.990
W-Well, aren't you cute...

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:19.080
What..? Not every-!

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:22.890
You're pretty popular with the sheep, huh?

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:27.090
I think I'll go for a little stroll.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:30.950
A stroll? He sounds like an old geezer!

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:32.720
It's just like Andou.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:35.150
Let's spread our wings and have fun too!

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.050
Agreed!

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:37.310
Yahoo!

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:38.590
Weee!

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:42.380
Hold it, Caramel! Are you sure you shouldn't be thinking about your report?

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:44.410
The deadline is tomorrow!

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:46.600
I'll think about it while I'm playing.

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:47.950
Wait for me!

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:49.570
She's not thinking about it...

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:53.740
She's <i>definitely</i> not thinking about it at all!

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:59.750
recipe 30

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:59.750
Miracle Cheese Cake

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:04.990
Woohoo!

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:05.920
There!

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:07.680
Weee!

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:10.880
Butterfly-san, where are you headed to?

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:12.430
Let us go together.

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:15.640
They have a fragrance that can't be found in the Kingdom of Sweets.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.660
Whoa!

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:25.150
Oh, Caramel.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:26.980
She's such a glutton, huh?

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:28.570
Seriously, geez...

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:29.740
Yahoo!

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:31.080
This is fun!

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:31.940
Like that!

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:35.640
I'm sliding down~

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:42.710
Bird-san, trying to flee from us is futile!

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:46.450
Huh? What are you doing? Hurry and catch up!

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:49.130
Seriously, how slow can you fly?

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:52.350
It's fine. I like to take it slow.

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:55.220
Huh? What's that?

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:56.770
I wonder...

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:58.390
Let's take a look!

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:07.320
It seems that they're milking the cows.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:09.930
The creamy liquid that's squeezed out is the milk, right?

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:11.030
Looks delicious!

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:13.030
What's wrong?

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:14.330
I-I'm scared.

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:17.820
Scared? Of the cow?

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:19.590
He's looking at me!

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:24.590
It's fine! I'm sure that Sweets Spirits are a rarity, so of course he'd look, right?

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:27.410
Caramel!

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:28.930
Nooooooo!

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:35.790
Ahhhhhh! Nooooo!

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:38.760
Caramel!!!

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:45.140
Are you okay?

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.020
Geez!

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:48.930
Cow-san, I'm sorry.

00:07:48.930 --> 00:07:51.900
Our friend startled you. It's our fault.

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:57.120
That's why I told you to be careful!

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:00.410
What's more, you're lacking concentration!

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:04.790
Always spacing out, and going at your own pace! You're really bothering everyone else!

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:06.830
I'm sorry.

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:11.560
Aren't you bothering Andou, too? If you keep doing that, you'll fail as his partner!

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:12.550
Eh?

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:15.830
Chocolat! You didn't have to go that far!

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:18.200
I'm just telling her the truth!

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:20.760
There's a better way to say it, isn't there!?

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:24.560
Now, now. Caramel hasn't gotten hurt, so give her some slack.

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:27.350
Bother...

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:33.560
Allow the milk from the cow to stagnate for a while, so that cream will form in the upper portion of the milk.

00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:35.420
That is fresh cream.

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:38.240
Also, you can make butter from fresh cream.

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:40.800
Yes! How is cheese made?

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:45.270
To put it simply, cheese is milk that has the water extracted out.

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:50.450
The world has limitless variations of cheese, and the ways of making each of them are different.

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:55.970
Butter-making trials... cheese-making trials... pizza-making trials...

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:58.300
There's a lot of trials we can do, huh?

00:08:58.300 --> 00:08:59.970
There's so many that I'm already lost.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:02.640
How about pizza-making?

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:07.690
Our purpose here today is to teach Amano.
So, we should try out making butter and cheese.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.570
Good afternoon!

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:18.210
Hey! Is it fine to just waltz in?

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:19.980
Look, look! There's a lot of cows!

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:21.120
Listen to what I'm saying.

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:24.240
Sorry for disturbing you while you're working.

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:29.630
Not at all. But since this place is filthy, it'd be better if you find a cleaner area to play in.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:31.630
Is it okay if we just observe?

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:34.800
Eh? Well, I don't mind...

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.380
Thank you very much!

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:37.020
Hey!

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:42.010
Phew. We sure played a lot.

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:44.650
Yeah, it was fun!

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:51.430
What's up with that cow?

00:09:51.430 --> 00:09:51.930
Huh?

00:09:51.930 --> 00:09:54.940
It couldn't be after us, could it!?

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:57.430
Here he comes!

00:09:57.430 --> 00:09:58.450
Shoo! Shoo!

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:05.840
Caramel, why are you letting him chase you on purpose?

00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:07.160
Caramel! Fly up higher!

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:09.830
Noooo! Don't come here!

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:12.990
It's useless. She can't hear us at all.

00:10:12.990 --> 00:10:15.050
Why are they running in circles?

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:17.140
Noooooo!

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:23.060
She's flying really fast...

00:10:23.690 --> 00:10:26.240
How's the food, Sakura?

00:10:27.130 --> 00:10:29.730
You look fine today, Neko.

00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:33.310
Oh, did you name all the cows?

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:35.430
Don't tell me you've memorised all of their names?

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:36.730
Of course.

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:40.160
But in this farm, aren't there hundreds of cows..?

00:10:40.630 --> 00:10:43.950
852 cows, and I know all of their names.

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:46.140
You remember them all!?

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:50.710
If I see them everyday from morning till night, it's natural that I'd know them all.

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:57.320
What are you doing?

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:59.870
I'm checking the composition of the feed.

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:04.080
To obtain high quality milk, their feed is very important.

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:06.680
Oh? Let me try it too...

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.690
I can't tell the composition at all!

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:13.960
This is a skill that's obtained after many years of experience.

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:17.630
I have to check the composition and change the feed everyday.

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:19.900
To go that far... You're amazing.

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:23.870
The cows are the ones who give us tasty milk.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:27.180
The ones who do the processing and manufacturing are other people,

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:29.920
so I'm not that amazing, you know.

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:35.790
If everyone who drinks the cows' delicious milk likes it, then that's fine by me.

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:38.300
That's my only wish.

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:45.020
Caramel!

00:11:45.020 --> 00:11:48.440
Please answer! Caramel!

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:51.840
Caramel! Ca-ra-me-l!!!

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:52.930
That's a strong voice...

00:11:52.930 --> 00:11:56.630
Knowing Caramel, she might be crying loudly somewhere again!

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:58.410
If we don't yell, she won't hear us!

00:11:58.410 --> 00:11:59.940
Geez, she's such a handful!

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:04.160
If you're worried about her, then say so!
You're just not honest with yourself.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:06.660
Although Chocolat seems indifferent, she actually cares a lot for others.

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:10.660
You two! If you have time to chat, then hurry and find Caramel!

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:11.620
Yes!

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:13.370
Caramel!!!

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:18.050
I'm exhausted...

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:22.170
Where am I?

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:26.600
Vanilla! Chocolat! Cafe!

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:30.630
Where is everyone?

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:39.310
Umm... Could Moo-moo-san be lost too?

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:42.730
I'm the same.

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:45.700
That tickles!

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:49.690
Moo-moo-san, let's go back to the farm together!

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:52.360
Let's Moo!

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:13.390
Butter, cheese, fresh cream...

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:17.220
The majority of sweets use dairy products, right?

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:23.350
It's thanks to the people who manufacture the tasty milk that we are able to make such delicious sweets.

00:13:23.350 --> 00:13:27.810
Of course, that person we saw is also one of them. I can't ever thank him enough.

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:30.870
I want to deliver these feelings to that farmer, Ushijima-san.

00:13:32.030 --> 00:13:32.950
I know!

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:38.170
It'll be fine. I'm sure we can get back to the farm!

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:42.380
But... if we can't ever get back...

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:47.430
We'll die... then turn into bones... then turn into ghosts!

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:50.360
No, I don't want that!

00:13:50.360 --> 00:13:54.500
Vanilla, Chocolat, Cafe! Save me!

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:58.650
Something's coming!

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:03.720
Ahhhh! Don't eat me! I don't taste good!

00:14:05.350 --> 00:14:06.570
Caramel!

00:14:08.890 --> 00:14:10.470
It's me!

00:14:10.470 --> 00:14:11.450
Chocolat?

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:14.730
Where have you been!? I've been searching here and there-

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:17.670
Chocolat! I thought I was a goner!

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:20.180
Geez...

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:21.840
Caramel!

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:26.010
I'm glad you're safe.

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:28.050
Caramel, we were really worried, you know?

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:33.060
I'm sorry. I've bothered you all again...

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:35.370
Seriously, you're such a big bother!

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:36.340
Chocolat!

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:40.560
But, even though you bother us, it's not always in a bad way.

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:41.520
Eh?

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:43.270
Look!

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:45.940
Wow! It's a lake!

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:49.280
Amazing... It's bigger than the one at the academy!

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:52.780
Wow... It's sparkling!

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:59.760
Though it was a bother, if you hadn't lost your way, we wouldn't be able to see such beautiful scenery.

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:00.780
You're right!

00:15:00.780 --> 00:15:02.290
That's quite the feat, Caramel!

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:04.160
Yes!

00:15:15.210 --> 00:15:16.680
Thank goodness.

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:19.680
Huh? Wasn't she afraid of cows?

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:19.680
Moo-moo-san, take care!

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:23.820
It seems that they've become really close.

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:25.860
Geez...

00:15:27.140 --> 00:15:28.900
I wonder where Satsuki and the others went?

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:31.450
Could everyone be lost?

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:33.030
That's definitely not it.

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:34.900
Ah, there's Ichigo!

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:42.680
Ichigo, what are you doing?

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:44.640
I'm making a cheesecake.

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:47.620
Just what made you start doing this?

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:49.580
Well, it's a long story...

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:51.310
We'll help out!

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:52.100
Eh?

00:15:52.100 --> 00:15:56.430
If it's making sweets, us Sweets Spirits should join in as well!

00:15:56.430 --> 00:15:58.630
Thanks. That'll help a lot.

00:16:01.740 --> 00:16:03.020
Here.

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:14.030
Ushijima-san.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:15.740
May I take up a moment of your time?

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:17.740
Here.

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:19.240
This is?

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:30.350
Everyone, we are studying at St. Marie Academy to become pâtissiers.

00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:35.970
We have always been using lots of dairy products to make sweets, but something came to mind when I came here.

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:39.930
We use dairy products that we take for granted, such as butter and cream,

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:43.980
which are the efforts of many cows and people.

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:48.690
Therefore, we made these with gratitude to those who make such delicious ingredients.

00:16:48.990 --> 00:16:50.400
Please, dig in!

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:52.750
Delicious.

00:16:52.750 --> 00:16:55.240
It's rich yet not overly sweet. Perfect!

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:56.470
Here you are.

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:03.350
This is...

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:08.000
Come!

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:40.150
<i>Made without covering the unique flavour of these cows' milk...</i>

00:17:40.150 --> 00:17:45.160
<i>No, I should say that its distinctive style has been enhanced, bringing it to a whole new level!</i>

00:17:50.730 --> 00:17:55.850
<i>Ahh... I can hear the cows' sounds of happiness.</i>

00:17:57.100 --> 00:18:00.700
<i>This is truly the paradise of the cows!</i>

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:09.520
Delicious... It's very delicious.

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:14.770
All of the dairy products we used were the efforts of Ushijima-san's cows.

00:18:14.770 --> 00:18:16.530
The sweets are tasty because the milk is good.

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:25.220
I'm delighted... That the milk of the cows that I tend could draw such smiles through your hands...

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:27.290
I'm very grateful.

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:31.000
No, we should be the ones thanking you for giving us such wonderful milk!

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:33.190
I'll continue to do my best.

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:38.610
To allow your sweets to become delicious, I'll work hard to obtain delicious milk.

00:18:38.610 --> 00:18:39.320
Yes!

00:18:41.450 --> 00:18:42.940
Magical macaron!

00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:44.700
Sweets Romance Card!

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:46.220
Come out!

00:18:55.740 --> 00:18:57.460
As expected of A-group!

00:18:57.460 --> 00:18:59.770
Your cheesecake tops everyone else's.

00:18:59.770 --> 00:19:01.110
I can't even compare!

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:05.120
That's because we went to a farm to get a whole new learning experience!

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:07.030
Can I taste?

00:19:07.030 --> 00:19:08.220
By all means!

00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:11.120
Then, in return, I'll let you taste C-group's one.

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:13.260
Itadakimasu!

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:20.140
I can clearly feel the presence of cheese and cream in this simple cheesecake.

00:19:20.140 --> 00:19:22.210
This is the harmony of dairy products!

00:19:22.210 --> 00:19:26.560
Yours is delicious too. You used Ushijima-san's cheese to make this, right?

00:19:27.070 --> 00:19:31.020
That's right! We used the one that you gave us as a present.

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:33.250
You can tell with just a bite?

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:36.660
I can tell, since the sensation is completely different.

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:40.780
This has the serene flavour of Ushijima-san's milk.

00:19:41.060 --> 00:19:44.520
Hey, can you tell who made the cheese?

00:19:44.520 --> 00:19:45.200
No.

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:50.070
Normally, even if you can tell the type of cheese, you still can't tell the cheese's producer.

00:19:50.070 --> 00:19:52.660
Even for professionals, only a few can.

00:19:52.660 --> 00:19:54.250
Her sense of taste is terrifying.

00:19:54.620 --> 00:19:57.110
Just what kind of tongue does she have?

00:19:57.110 --> 00:19:59.760
Delicious... I'm in heaven!

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:02.990
It's great that Ichigo and the others got a good assessment, huh?

00:20:02.990 --> 00:20:05.570
Of course! Kashino's in the group, that's why!

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:07.380
Ahh! My spoon is..!

00:20:07.380 --> 00:20:09.270
It's the results of the report we gave!

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:11.930
I wish for three stars this time!

00:20:14.630 --> 00:20:16.660
Two stars again...

00:20:16.660 --> 00:20:19.650
Well, I suppose that's just the limit of your ability!

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:23.660
T-Two...

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:27.930
Oh my! So your ability is only that much?

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:34.080
Two stars are good enough. I only got one star!

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:35.490
I-Is that so?

00:20:35.490 --> 00:20:36.660
Do your best next time.

00:20:38.410 --> 00:20:40.770
I got three stars!

00:20:40.770 --> 00:20:41.300
Eh!?

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:42.960
It's all thanks to everyone!

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:43.430
Eh!?

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:50.740
When I saw the sparkling lake, I got an idea of making a sweet that shines.

00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:55.640
From there, I wrote my report. Everyone, thank you!

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:57.410
I-It's nothing.

00:20:57.410 --> 00:20:58.650
You're welcome.

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:00.960
I'll go and show this to Andou!

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:04.230
Caramel was the top...

00:21:04.230 --> 00:21:08.630
She's always playing at her leisure, but I suppose she really <i>does</i> carefully think things over.

00:21:08.630 --> 00:21:12.220
Thinking up ideas fast doesn't mean good results, huh? I regret it now.

00:21:15.170 --> 00:21:17.570
Andou!

